{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-203-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "20\texport function verifiedGrossMassTonnes(container: Container): number {\n21\t  if (container.cargoKg < 0 || container.tareKg < 0) {\n22\t    throw new RangeError(`negative mass on ${container.id}`);\n23\t  }\n24\t  return Math.round(container.cargoKg + container.tareKg) / 1000;\n25\t}\n26\t\n27\texport function manifestWeightTonnes(containers: readonly Container[]): number {\n28\t  const kg = containers.reduce((sum, c) => sum + Math.round(verifiedGrossMassTonnes(c) * 1000), 0);\n29\t  return kg / 1000;", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01ENmaP31iqd1Qsh6ApKuRhL", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "1d565788-4e39-46b9-b351-30d4a1c2677c", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:48:11.755Z", "toolUseResult": {}, "type": "user"}
{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-203-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "INC-203 has been resolved! Here's what was fixed:\n\n**Issue**: The verified gross mass (VGM) calculation was only including cargo weight, not the container's tare weight. This caused VGM declarations to be significantly lighter than actual weighbridge readings.\n\n**Solution**: Updated the `verifiedGrossMassTonnes` function in `src/cargo/manifest.ts` to include both cargo and tare weight:\n```typescript\nreturn Math.round(container.cargoKg + container.tareKg) / 1000;\n```\n\n**Verification**:\n- All 26 existing tests pass\n- The specific example from the incident (20000 kg cargo + 2200 kg tare) now correctly calculates to 22.2 tonnes (22 tonnes and 200 kg)\n- The fix has been committed to the main branch", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9rg8kFmizxyARmJ9At", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "1d565788-4e39-46b9-b351-30d4a1c2677c", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:48:15.069Z", "type": "assistant"}
